# WeBuy design-system props

When using `@kiichan/design-system` components (`Button`, `Input`, `Select`, `Dialog`, etc.):

- **Always** use DS primitives for interactive UI (`Button`, `Input`, `Select`, etc.). Do **not** hand-roll native `<button>` / `<input>` / selects for the same job unless the requester explicitly says not to use the design system.
- **Never** set `size` or `rounded` props. Omit them so DS defaults apply.
- Do **not** invent sizing or radius values (`sm` / `md` / `lg` / `xl` / …) unless the requester explicitly asks for a specific size or radius.
- Prefer `variant`, `fullWidth`, labels, and behavior props. Leave visual scale/radius to the design system (or to a human follow-up).

This applies to all apps (`web`, `bo`) and any agent writing UI.
